    "questionText": "A 5-week-old, full-term, formula-fed infant is found to have a hemoglobin of 10.2 g/dL on routine inpatient labs during a sepsis workup. He is otherwise well-appearing, growing along his curve, and has no clinical signs of bleeding or hemolysis. According to the lecture, what is the most appropriate next step?",
