      { "text": "Ristocetin-induced platelet aggregation.", "explanation": "Incorrect. Ristocetin testing diagnoses vWD or Bernard-Soulier syndrome; the patient's pattern is not consistent with these. This would be the correct answer if the patient had mild mucosal bleeding with abnormal ristocetin testing." },
      { "text": "Heparin-PF4 antibody assay.", "explanation": "Incorrect. This diagnoses HIT, which requires recent heparin exposure. This would be the correct answer if the patient had been on heparin and developed thrombocytopenia with thrombosis." }
